abstract: >-
  DATect is a one-week-ahead quantitative forecasting system for domoic acid (DA)
  contamination of shellfish at 10 monitoring sites along the U.S. Pacific Northwest
  coast. One random forest with shared settings at every site is retrained for each
  forecast on past weeks only, with observation-order lag features for sparse,
  irregular DA measurements. A spike classifier pooled across sites adds an
  early-warning alert, and an 80% conformal band gives each forecast a range.
  Evaluation is leak-free and chronological: every real measurement in 2022-2023 is
  scored, with bootstrap confidence intervals. That window has not been a tuning
  objective since the protocol was fixed in May 2026, but it has been read repeatedly
  to check changes.
